By the Law of Cosines again, \begin{align*} \cos B &= \frac{c^2 + a^2 - b^2}{2ca} = \frac{16 + 4 - 9}{2 \cdot 4 \cdot 2} = \frac{11}{16}, \text{so} \\ 2 \angle B &= 2 \arccos \left( \frac{11}{16} \right) \approx 27.68^\circ. \end{align*} Adding the two expressions, we get $3 \angle A + 2 \angle B \approx 137.12^\circ$. The answer is $\boxed{137}$ (rounding to the nearest integer).
