\left(\dfrac{h - 2}{h}\right)^2 = \dfrac{1}{2}.
\end{align*} Squaring both sides and expanding the brackets, we get \begin{align*} 
h^2 - 4h + 4 = \dfrac{h^2}{2}, \end{align*} which simplifies to \begin{align*} 
\dfrac{h^2}{2} - 4h + 4 = 0. \end{align*} Multiplying both sides by 2, we get \begin{align*} 
h^2 - 8h + 8 = 0. \end{align*} Using the quadratic formula, we find that the solutions are $ h = 4 \pm 2 \sqrt2 $. Since $ h \ge 2$, we take $ h = 4 + 2 \sqrt2 $, which simplifies to $ \boxed{6} $ units. </think> <answer> $6$ </answer>

