\begin{align*}
y &= a(x^2 - (m+n)x + mn) \\
&= ax^2 - a(m+n)x + amn
\end{align*}
Comparing with the original equation, we have:
\begin{align*}
b &= -a(m+n) \\
c &= amn
\end{align*}
We also know that the vertex of the parabola is at the point $(2,1)$. The x-coordinate of the vertex is given by $-\frac{b}{2a}$. Substituting the values we found for $b$ from above, we have:
\begin{align*}
2 &= -\frac{b}{2a} \\
2 &= -\frac{-a(m+n)}{2a} \\
2 &= \frac{m+n}{2} \\
4 &= m+n
\end{align*}

The y-coordinate of the vertex is given by $f\left(-\frac{b}{2a}\right) = 1$. Substituting the values we found for $b$ from above, we have:
\begin{align*}
1 &= a\left(2^2 - (m+n)2 + mn\right) \\
1 &= a\left(4 - 4 + mn\right) \\
1 &= amn
\end{align*}

We now have two equations:
\begin{align*}
m+n &= 4 \\
mn &= \frac{1}{a}
\end{align*}

